From 6083a4b85025de2a2e6b92b6ba8d6fb85b78c013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaNan <1607702@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:43:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plm-qt): scale fixed UI sizes with font size and clamp
 font range

The Qt frontend broke when a large font size (e.g. 18.5 px) was saved
in settings: the fixed-width sidebar, lane grid, and tables were sized
against a 13 px baseline and could not fit the larger text, causing
overflow and clipped content.

- Clamp Settings font size to 11-16 px and apply the same clamp in
  MainWindow._apply_font().
- Introduce _ui_scale() helpers and scale hardcoded widths/heights in
  sidebar, topbar, tab bar, lane grid, and EditableTable.
- Replace the lane grid palette bar's QHBoxLayout with a wrapping
  _FlowLayout so swatches reflow instead of overflowing at narrow
  widths or larger fonts.
- Scale lane grid palette swatch padding/radius from the baseline.

Fixes the layout issues visible in the work/ debug screenshots when
font size was set to 18.5 px.
